ke. From you, that&#x27;s four hundred and six leads, twenty one percent conversion, sixty two mortgage applications, thirty four renewal cases, forty insurances. Ninety one admin. Your average admin fee at the moment is quite strong at seven six one. Average renewals at seven two four. Average protection of one three and then average admin fee of two four nine, and you&#x27;ve got a cut.</p><p>Speaker 2: Conversion ninety three and fifty percent in a random forty, which is slightly lower. That&#x27;s because one of the re mortgage cases might only be one in four changes, whereas on the purchase, you&#x27;d expect it to be about a one in three average. Those numbers are then pulled over into here. So that provides you with your bank target, your written target. And then what I am looking for everybody to do is to fill this in month by month, and what I would see is fill it in weekly prior to the check-in. What have you written? What have you banked? And then how many purchase cases have been actioned and delivered? And then that be populated so all the other fields such as Q one, Q two. The other thing that we&#x27;ve got in here is the remortgage opportunities. So again, this shows total opportunities for the year, but it isn&#x27;t taken into account the fact that we&#x27;re.</p><p>Speaker 2: Aiming to get sixty percent conversion, but what we are going to do is track the conversion over the year just to see. Are we actually on target? Are we converting sixty percent? Is there a reason that we&#x27;re not converting sixty percent? What&#x27;s the outcome? Are they just not getting booked in or are they getting booked in, but they&#x27;re not going anywhere? But what is going on with them? And then the final piece, which has a report that Graham has got built as leads. So how many leads are coming in? What&#x27;s happening with them? And where are we going with them? So what I&#x27;ve put on the back of that email, which I&#x27;m just going to bring up just now, wh