average case 183.</p><p>Speaker 2: So it&#x27;s relatively good numbers, but how do we now grow that and really build on that this year? So all the numbers are there for you to look at. And then finally, I just want to touch on what you&#x27;ve got in pipeline because obviously, that&#x27;s already going to put you off to a good start into the new financial year. The more you managed to write end of last year going into this year, it means that you are going into this year with a bit of a foot up. You think about if you want to bank one hundred and eighty, you&#x27;ve actually got just shy of fifty k already in the bank. But that&#x27;s not to mean that you don&#x27;t want to write one hundred and eighty or two hundred thousand; you want to because then that&#x27;s putting that pipeline back into next year. It&#x27;s a next year pipeline and it&#x27;s getting you off to that good start. So if we&#x27;re looking at Q one so far.</p><p>Speaker 2: We got thirty one k in the pot already. Big number. How do you maintain that? That&#x27;s going to be the key thing. So really have a rethink about those. And the big thing that I guess we&#x27;re really going to be focusing this year is on leads and the leads across the whole business. So myself and Alan are really going to be working quite closely with all of the teams this year, pretty much on a monthly basis to drive the opportunities. There&#x27;s going to be a real focus on getting to that magic forty. Then once we get to that magic forty, what we&#x27;re hoping for is for you to be able to speak to thirty customers. Those thirty customers, the industry average is a one in three conversion. Which ironically is exactly where we finished last year of one in three conversion across the board for everybody. A little bit higher some, a little bit lower than others. But if you had the industry average which is one in three.</p><p>Speaker 2: That&#x27;s what we want to get to. Can you imagine? We deliver it this year or we rea