ales. We didn&#x27;t increase any targets last year, even though we had the national insurance uplift. But obviously, this year, we now are carrying one side as part of that.</p><p>Speaker 2: Slightly tweaking everyone&#x27;s monthly bank target. At the moment, do five roles. That&#x27;s just been around to seven five before, so a very small increase. But the key thing here for this year, and I would ask everybody to really focus on is that the big aim is for us to get you forty appointments in your diary every single month. Then the big focus from there is making sure the quality is good on these meetings that are there as well. Are we getting the right leads and working with the team to make sure the contact with insurance is good? Once that&#x27;s managed, what you need to focus on is converting these into one. If you can get fourteen new leads a month every month, you will exceed the target that&#x27;s been set, which you set yourself already. Because the target that you&#x27;ve set is basically maintaining the same number of output to the same number of.</p><p>Speaker 2: The same conversion rate to the same one, go and based on your remortgage, you&#x27;re going to see it&#x27;s not that target. The big focus this year is actually for me now is to drive more opportunities with diary. But we need to focus on quality in the output of those, and then that client says, &quot;Are you doing your best?&quot; Are you in touch? We convert on the one in three because if you do that. You will actually exceed what you&#x27;ve aimed to deliver this year yourself.</p><p>Paul Banyard: Are you saying that instead of having to bank eighteen thousand seven hundred and fifty before you start earning any, you start earning twenty percent of the banks?</p><p>Paul Banyard: It&#x27;s going up to twenty-one thousand seven hundred and fifty. It&#x27;s gone up by three thousand. Is that what you&#x27;re saying?</p><p>Speaker 2: Yeah. Okay.</p><p>Speaker 2: Make sense. And then the only 