aker 2: Such and such is going to be calling me today at ten o&#x27;clock. And being in touch with me and that, but such and such has texted me. Have you seen anything? They&#x27;re much more likely to reply to that text message than probably your chance of phone in an email. I am not saying you shouldn&#x27;t. But what I am saying is, are we making use of all of the things that are available?</p><p>Paul Banyard: You got two. You got to move on. You have two seconds to look at the platform.</p><p>Speaker 2: I think I&#x27;m meant to be in another call, but let me double check. I am meant to be in McLaren, but I can have a quick look because Claire&#x27;s will be fairly straightforward.</p><p>Paul Banyard: Just added this lead.</p><p>Speaker 1: O&#x27;Farrell and that&#x27;s Craig&#x27;s that&#x27;s fine.</p><p>Paul Banyard: Yep, when I was updating the lead Christ, it&#x27;s getting used to where everything is.</p><p>Speaker 2: It is,</p><p>Paul Banyard: How do you? What are you trying to do? I managed the lead source. Click on the client directory.</p><p>Speaker 2: Client name.</p><p>Paul Banyard: That&#x27;s the thing; it&#x27;s like sometimes you need to click on client names, sometimes you don&#x27;t.</p><p>Speaker 2: I don&#x27;t think you want to go into that one if you scroll down a wee bit. Nope, not that one either. Lead status. And yeah, give it that one. It&#x27;s not that. That&#x27;s cancel. And source, scroll down and keep going down. Click on manage leads and then where it says manage tasks and workflow, click on that one.</p><p>Speaker 1: The latest one that I sent you there.</p><p>Speaker 2: The reason I was showing you. This is when I was adding the lead source, it wouldn&#x27;t let me put my name in. It only had a drop down. It had your name and it had loads of people I&#x27;d never heard of. So there&#x27;s no way, I&#x27;m guessing the reporting still works the same. There&#x27;s no way saying this is a self generated lead by Paul Banyard. There